  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Let's draw the actual price level since twenty twenty, honestly, because the headlines keep saying inflation is beaten.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "coin"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Prices since",
            "2020."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Inflation did cool from its peak. But cooling inflation only means prices climb slower, not that they fall.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "kicker": "the key distinction",
          "line": "Slower ≠ cheaper",
          "sub": "the level never came back down"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Inflation is the rate the average price of goods and services goes up.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-inflation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · inflation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Stacked up since twenty twenty, the cumulative rise is roughly twenty percent on everyday goods.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "~20%",
          "label": "higher prices since 2020",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The CPI tracks that level, and the line just keeps grinding upward.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-cpi",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · consumer price index"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Zoom out further and about eighty-five percent of the nineteen seventy dollar's value is already gone.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "big": "~85%",
          "label": "of the 1970 dollar, gone",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And where prices can't rise, the package quietly shrinks instead.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-shrink",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · shrinkflation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The dollar is, by design, a slowly melting ice cube.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "A melting dollar",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So every single year you hold plain cash, a little more of its value quietly melts away for good.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Cash melts",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ]
